course: dictionary
lesson: 1526
title: CEO: the top boss
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: CEO is an abbreviation, a short form of longer words. It stands for Chief Executive Officer. Its plural is CEOs, and it is a noun, a name for a person.
explain: «A CEO is the top boss of a company.» The CEO is the most important manager. They make the big decisions, lead the other managers, and answer to a board of directors.
explain: The next sentence gives you more clues: «a CEO on £2,000,000 a year earns 100 times as much as a worker on £20,000.» The big numbers show that a CEO earns far more than a worker. Some people think bosses earn it, but others think it is unfair, so people can disagree about it.
fact: CEO stands for Chief Executive Officer.
fact: A CEO is the most important manager of a company or organisation.
fact: A CEO makes the big decisions and leads the other managers.
fact: A CEO answers to a board of directors.
fact: Other people may joke, «I'm the CEO of snacks», meaning they are in charge of snacks.
exercise: «A CEO is the top boss of a company.» What does CEO stand for? | Company Entry Officer | *Chief Executive Officer | Central Email Office | Chief Excellent Owner
exercise: «a CEO on £2,000,000 a year earns 100 times as much as a worker on £20,000.» How many times more does the CEO earn? | 1,000 times | 2,000 times | 10 times | *100 times
exercise: Which best describes a CEO? | A worker who earns £20,000 a year | A cleaner who looks after the offices | A type of computer game | *The top manager who makes the big decisions
test: «Both CEOs agreed to the new plan.» How many CEOs agreed? | One | None | *Two | Ten
test: A friend says, «I'm the CEO of snacks.» What does the joke mean? | *I am in charge of snacks | I do not like snacks | I am the dog of a snack shop | I make snacks in a factory
exam: Some say bosses earn it, others say it is unfair. What does this tell you about CEO pay? | CEOs earn the same as workers | *People have different opinions about it | Nobody talks about it | Everyone agrees it is fair
